cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: netfault
abstract: >-
  A fault dictionary for linear analog circuits. Given a netlist and a
  measured frequency response, it simulates every single-component fault
  that could explain the measurement and ranks them, naming the part and
  the factor. Includes a numpy modified-nodal-analysis solver, so a linear
  dictionary is built without an external simulator, and reports when no
  candidate explains the measurement rather than returning a confident
  wrong answer.
type: software
